Postfix on FenrirOS
===================

Installed inert: the service is not enabled, nothing listens, no aliases
database, certificates or SASL secrets are made.

Layout: configuration /etc/postfix (main.cf and master.cf as upstream ships
them; *.proto are the pristine copies), commands /usr/sbin, daemons
/usr/libexec/postfix, private libraries and map plugins /usr/lib/postfix,
queue /var/spool/postfix, data /var/lib/postfix. Mail owner _postfix, setgid
group _postdrop (both from sysusers.d). Default database type: lmdb (no
Berkeley DB), so "hash:" maps are "lmdb:" here.

Map types: lmdb, pcre (PCRE2), regexp, texthash, inline, ... in the main
package; ldap, mysql (MariaDB), pgsql and sqlite are the postfix-ldap,
postfix-mysql, postfix-pgsql and postfix-sqlite packages. SMTPUTF8 (ICU),
TLS (OpenSSL), SASL: Dovecot's (smtpd_sasl_type = dovecot) and Cyrus
libsasl (for the SMTP client and smtpd_sasl_type = cyrus).

1. Set myhostname, mydomain, mydestination, inet_interfaces, mynetworks in
   /etc/postfix/main.cf (postconf -e name=value). The stock main.cf listens
   on every interface once started; inet_interfaces = loopback-only for a
   send-only host.
2. TLS: put your certificate and key somewhere and set smtpd_tls_chain_files
   (and smtpd_tls_security_level = may, smtp_tls_security_level = may).
3. Aliases: edit /etc/postfix/aliases (root's mail to a real user), set
   alias_maps = lmdb:/etc/postfix/aliases, alias_database likewise, then
   run newaliases.
4. Submission/SMTPS with SASL through Dovecot: uncomment the submission and
   smtps entries of master.cf and set smtpd_sasl_type = dovecot,
   smtpd_sasl_path = private/auth (Dovecot's auth socket for Postfix).
5. postfix check; postfix set-permissions (sets owners and modes the
   package could not, for example after an upgrade); then
   dinitctl enable postfix.

Only one MTA can be installed: postfix, opensmtpd and exim each own
/usr/sbin/sendmail, /usr/bin/mailq and /usr/bin/newaliases.
